From da3c1093042008fab5ed5df2366aed3c39f9d23b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:43:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(players): transport remote movement modes and targets

Official Bedrock 1.26.60.5, protocol 2225, smooths admitted normal moves
through three float-rounded positions, including large excursions.
Java position packets lose the source mode and apply a different curve.
Java rotation-only packets also quantize pitch and omit the head target.

Publish a negotiated receipt before each remote player's translated
position or rotation packet. Retain native inputs, source mode, known
riding, UUID, lifetime, raw actor flags and unsigned duration. Carry the
exact Java target separately, including its packet family. Preserve the
existing float/double Y arithmetic and byte-angle translation so pairing
does not depend on reconstructing either packet family's rounding.

Keep raw head-only position, pitch and head yaw. Its supplied position
and conflicting main yaw remain inert for position and main yaw. The
outer native packet handler 0x146bd39a0 derives motion from raw packet
position minus the previous StateVector before mode dispatch. Current native mode helper
0x1402d92c0 leaves pending position and main-rotation targets intact,
applies pitch immediately, and refreshes the independent head counter.
The client can reproduce this branch without changing legacy packets.

Consume receipts once in connection order. Retire unmatched batches and
bound pending state so modes cannot cross packet, actor or connection
lifetimes. Exclude local players, generic actors and unavailable native
state. Keep absolute/delta receive caches and collision history separate
from normal player movement and client interpolation.
